### Topic 35 - Global Exception Handling
### Run the app in any profile (default / problem / plain) and compare the error JSON.

@base = http://localhost:8080/api/books

### 1. OK - list books
GET {{base}}

### 2. 404 - book does not exist (ResourceNotFoundException)
GET {{base}}/99

### 3. 400 - id is not a number (MethodArgumentTypeMismatchException)
GET {{base}}/abc

### 4. 400 - validation failed (MethodArgumentNotValidException) -> fieldErrors
POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "", "author": "X", "isbn": "123", "copies": -1 }

### 5. 409 - duplicate ISBN (DuplicateResourceException)
POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Clean Code again", "author": "Robert C. Martin", "isbn": "9780132350884", "copies": 1 }

### 6. 400 - broken JSON (HttpMessageNotReadableException)
POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "broken

### 7. 201 - a valid new book
POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Spring in Action", "author": "Craig Walls", "isbn": "9781617297571", "copies": 3 }

### 8. 200 then 422 - borrow "Effective Java" (1 copy) twice
POST {{base}}/2/borrow

### 9. 422 - "Head First Java" has 0 copies (BookNotAvailableException)
POST {{base}}/3/borrow

### 10. 400 - query parameter constraint (HandlerMethodValidationException)
GET {{base}}/available?minCopies=0

### 11. 405 - DELETE not supported on the collection URL
DELETE {{base}}

### 12. 404 - unknown URL (NoResourceFoundException)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/bookz

### 13. 500 - simulated bug: generic message, NO stack trace to the client
GET {{base}}/crash
